WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.509
Mary and Dickon worked in the secret garden all morning.

2
00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:11.235
When Mary went inside for lunch, she ate quickly.

3
00:00:11.236 --> 00:00:15.614
"Tell Colin I can't come right now," she said to Martha.

4
00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:18.897
"I'm too busy working in the garden with Dickon."

5
00:00:18.898 --> 00:00:25.322
Martha looked frightened. "Oh, that will put him in a bad mood."

6
00:00:25.323 --> 00:00:28.430
But Mary didn't care.

7
00:00:28.431 --> 00:00:33.751
She ran back to the secret garden, where Dickon was digging with his own shovel.

8
00:00:33.752 --> 00:00:39.852
They worked all afternoon. The fox and crow were busy too.

9
00:00:39.853 --> 00:00:44.247
Sometimes the crow flapped its wings and flew out of the garden.

10
00:00:44.248 --> 00:00:53.091
Each time it returned, it perched near Dickon and cawed as if it were telling them about its adventures.

11
00:00:53.092 --> 00:00:58.278
When Mary wanted to rest a bit, Dickon sat down with her under a tree.

12
00:00:58.279 --> 00:01:01.663
He took out his pipe and began to play.

13
00:01:01.664 --> 00:01:06.676
Two squirrels appeared on top of the wall to watch and listen.

14
00:01:06.677 --> 00:01:10.463
After a while the children went back to work.

15
00:01:10.464 --> 00:01:14.852
The sun was beginning to set when they finally decided to stop.

16
00:01:14.853 --> 00:01:18.865
"I'll see you at dawn tomorrow," said Dickon.

17
00:01:18.866 --> 00:01:21.880
Mary ran back to the house.

18
00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:26.071
She could hardly wait to tell Colin about Dickon's fox and crow.

19
00:01:26.072 --> 00:01:30.233
But when Mary arrived at her room, Martha was waiting.

20
00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:33.660
"I wish you'd gone to see Colin today.

21
00:01:33.661 --> 00:01:37.742
He's been on the verge of a tantrum all afternoon."

22
00:01:37.743 --> 00:01:40.757
Mary pinched her lips together.

23
00:01:40.758 --> 00:01:46.170
She saw no reason why a bad-tempered boy should interfere with what she enjoyed.

24
00:01:46.171 --> 00:01:49.722
She marched down the corridor in a sour mood.

25
00:01:49.723 --> 00:01:54.751
When she entered his room, Colin was not sitting up on his sofa.

26
00:01:54.752 --> 00:01:58.598
Instead he was lying in bed.

27
00:01:58.599 --> 00:02:01.055
"Why are you in bed?"

28
00:02:01.056 --> 00:02:06.672
"I got up this morning when I thought you were coming," Colin said without looking at her.

29
00:02:06.673 --> 00:02:10.899
"This afternoon I asked the servants to put me back in bed.

30
00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:17.452
My back ached and my head ached and I was tired. Why didn't you come?"

31
00:02:17.453 --> 00:02:20.620
"I was working in the garden with Dickon."

32
00:02:20.621 --> 00:02:26.989
Colin frowned. "I won't let that boy in here if you stay with him instead of coming to talk to me."

33
00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:34.379
Now Mary was angry. "If you do that, I'll never come into this room again."

34
00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.433
"You'll have to if I want you to."

35
00:02:37.434 --> 00:02:41.355
"I won't!" Mary stamped her foot.

36
00:02:41.356 --> 00:02:44.599
"I'll make you. They'll drag you in."

37
00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:51.163
"Will they, Mr. Rajah? They can drag me in, but they can't make me talk!

38
00:02:51.164 --> 00:02:55.144
I'll sit and clench my teeth and never tell you one thing.

39
00:02:55.145 --> 00:02:59.376
I won't even look at you. I'll stare at the floor!"

40
00:02:59.377 --> 00:03:01.855
They glared at each other.

41
00:03:01.856 --> 00:03:05.789
"You're a selfish thing!" cried Colin.

42
00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:10.833
Mary's eyes flashed with fire. "And so are you!"

43
00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:14.577
"I'm not as selfish as your perfect Dickon is.

44
00:03:14.578 --> 00:03:18.306
He keeps you outside when I need you here.

45
00:03:18.307 --> 00:03:22.579
And I'm not as selfish as you are because I'm always ill.

46
00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:27.288
I'm sure there's a lump coming on my back, and I'm going to die!"

47
00:03:27.289 --> 00:03:29.961
"Oh, you are not!"

48
00:03:29.962 --> 00:03:37.274
Colin opened his eyes wide. No one had ever said anything like that to him.

49
00:03:37.275 --> 00:03:43.118
"You know I am!" he said. "Everybody says so."

50
00:03:43.119 --> 00:03:46.821
"You just say that to make people feel sorry for you.

51
00:03:46.822 --> 00:03:49.399
I believe you're proud of it."

52
00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:54.017
In spite of his bad back, Colin sat up in bed.

53
00:03:54.018 --> 00:03:59.126
"Get out of this room!" He threw his pillow at her.

54
00:03:59.127 --> 00:04:02.310
"I'm going, and I won't come back."

55
00:04:02.311 --> 00:04:06.513
She walked to the door, but then she turned around.

56
00:04:06.514 --> 00:04:11.884
"I was going to tell you all sorts of nice things about Dickon's fox and crow.

57
00:04:11.885 --> 00:04:14.981
But now I won't tell you anything."

58
00:04:14.982 --> 00:04:17.990
She stormed back to her room.

59
00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:22.988
Martha was waiting for her, but this time the housemaid was smiling.

60
00:04:22.989 --> 00:04:25.962
"Look what Mr. Craven sent!"

61
00:04:25.963 --> 00:04:31.289
There on the table was a wooden box full of neatly wrapped packages.

62
00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.202
Mary sat down and opened them.

63
00:04:34.203 --> 00:04:40.783
Mr. Craven had sent her picture books and games and a beautiful pen and inkstand.

64
00:04:40.784 --> 00:04:46.151
If she hadn't been fighting with Colin, she would have run to show him everything.

65
00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:49.861
They would have read the books and played with the games.

66
00:04:49.862 --> 00:04:56.001
He would have enjoyed himself so much, he would have forgotten all about checking for lumps.

67
00:04:56.002 --> 00:05:02.424
"He always begins to think about that when he's tired or upset," Mary said to herself.

68
00:05:02.425 --> 00:05:08.443
"He's upset today. Maybe he's been thinking about his back all afternoon."

69
00:05:08.444 --> 00:05:11.474
She looked at her pile of presents.

70
00:05:11.475 --> 00:05:16.044
"I said I'd never go back, but maybe I'll go in the morning."

71
00:05:16.045 --> 00:05:23.165
She'd try to see him—even if he did throw his pillow at her again.

